This is a Rocq formalization of a simplified version of the Ur programming
language (Featherweight Ur): the syntax of kinds, constructors and
expressions, the definitional equality and disjointness rules on rows, and a
denotational model in which every rule is proved sound and every well-typed
expression has a denotation (Semantics.v: deq_correct, disj_correct, eDen).
Its only axiom is functional extensionality (Axioms.v).

Diff.v is a sketch of row difference (`c1 -- c2`, constructor CDiff) on top
of it: inter and union defined from it, a difference computed by the rules,
and the set laws as derivations in deq.  At kind {Unit} they come from the
rule Eq_Unit, which asks Sets.v's decision procedure; Sets.v proves it sound
and complete for the model, so every equation of [], ++ and -- at {Unit}
that holds there is derivable.  Through a row's names they reach
differences at any kind: cutting in either order gives the same row.

Checked with Rocq 9.1.1 and rocq-stdlib 9.0.0, as pinned in nixpkgs.nix:

    nix-shell --pure --run make    # or nix-build

It was originally written for Coq 8.3pl2.
